  "sge_audit": {
    "explanation": "In Phase 13, permuted predictions and targets were directly reshaped into (8, 8) grids without inverse coordinate un-shuffling. Because random spatial coordinate permutation scatters adjacent grid points across the field, the true gradient denominator ||nabla Y_pi||_F becomes massively inflated due to high-frequency discontinuities across adjacent permuted cells. Consequently, the ratio ||nabla Y_pi - nabla \\hat{Y}_pi||_F / ||nabla Y_pi||_F artificially drops from 0.59 to 0.28 purely as an artifact of the scrambled denominator. When evaluated in the true physical coordinate space (by un-permuting coordinates before computing spatial derivatives), the spatial gradient error of permutation-equivariant models is exactly identical to the original unpermuted SGE."
